{"title":"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A company sells rectangular business cards. Each card has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773364718d825a37e31cda99985c2e0ca46e0730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ cm} \\times 9 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. Cards are printed on a page and then the page is cut to produce the individual cards.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of each business card in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce95ec3eb5f2ff5452281e5b03c39757b163de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the dimensions of the paper, the width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fc08a0e2ab07fd633e0b872263f2dc3fe8e1917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> and the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/28881fe3b94b745f58e68198bcaa10724e6ba875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. Using the formula for the area of a rectangle, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92f4ae4187c7723abfe1de9375a07354db80e8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 20 \\text { cm} \\times 27 \\text { cm} = \\boxed{540 \\text{ cm}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"249\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Next, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a>'s answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/518a93a06c6869d715971fc337bc0dcac84b6126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\text{ cm}^{ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5e2b75853cf43b620ad21b6742838f27cf63a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540 \\text { cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> into this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c689d048d670d46cae20fbcfac865ca461ec5030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{540 \\text { cm}^{2}}{45 \\text { cm}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/75850a4440ad027141ee6eefae85f6fa355a6107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the paper's width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/9/8a9e12af1319525f6ecfe274643cad01d2aacf7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20 \\text { cm}}{5 \\text { cm}} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> times the width of each card. Similarly, we see that the paper's height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c3d7c87f0e584693614812a29767a03914da66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{27 \\text{ cm}}{9 \\text { cm}} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> times the height of each card.\n</p><p>Thus, the area of the card is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0100e092144beb8e883f065cc25075636e435a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 3 = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" /> business cards.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014432\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 66/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2382/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.255      1 2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.255      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35542:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018014432 and revision id 277869. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}